# 2FA setup checklist (backend)

> Generated by `auth:setup`. Do these steps, tick them, then delete this file. How 2FA works: https://github.com/Light-it-labs/lightit-auth-laravel/blob/main/docs/google-2fa.md

- [ ] **Wire the challenge into `LoginAction`** (`src/Authentication/Domain/Actions/LoginAction.php`): inject it in
  the constructor, then call it right after `$request->session()->regenerate();`, before `return $user;`.

```php
{{gateConstructorSnippet}}
```

```php
{{gateCallSnippet}}
```

- [ ] **Make `User` support 2FA** (`src/Users/Domain/Models/User.php`): `\Lightit\Users\Domain\Models\User` must extend
  `\Lightit\Authentication\Domain\TwoFactorAuthenticatable`. Replace `use Illuminate\Foundation\Auth\User as Authenticatable;`
  with `use Lightit\Authentication\Domain\TwoFactorAuthenticatable;`, and `extends Authenticatable` with `extends TwoFactorAuthenticatable`.
- [ ] **Run `php artisan migrate`** (adds the 2FA columns to `users`).
- [ ] **Pick the mode** in `.env`: `TWO_FACTOR_AUTHENTICATION_MANDATORY=true` (default: every user sets 2FA up at login)
  or `false` (users turn it on from `/account/two-factor`).

Check it worked: log in. With `true` the response is `200` with `token_type: setup_required`; with `false` a user
without 2FA comes straight in.
